{"title":"GK","timeMinutes":10,"questions":[{"text":"Which of the following is NOT one of the four fundamental forces of nature?","image":"","options":["Centrifugal force","Weak nuclear force","Strong nuclear force","Electromagnetic force"],"correctIdx":0},{"text":"Which ancient civilization developed the earliest known writing system, cuneiform?","image":"","options":["Ancient China","Indus Valley Civilization","Ancient Egypt","Sumerian civilization"],"correctIdx":3},{"text":"Which of the following numbers is irrational?","image":"","options":["√49","√2","7/8","0.25"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"Which economist wrote The General Theory of Employment, Interest and Money?","image":"","options":["John Maynard Keynes","David Ricardo","Milton Friedman","Adam Smith"],"correctIdx":0},{"text":"Which particle mediates the electromagnetic force?","image":"","options":["Gluon","Higgs boson","Photon","Neutrino"],"correctIdx":2},{"text":"Which of the following countries has no permanent natural rivers?","image":"","options":["Mongolia","Saudi Arabia","Iran","Iraq"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"Which mathematical constant is the base of natural logarithms?","image":"","options":["e","φ (the golden ratio)","√2","π"],"correctIdx":0},{"text":"Which scientist proposed the theory of continental drift in 1912?","image":"","options":["James Hutton","Harry Hess","Charles Lyell","Alfred Wegener"],"correctIdx":3},{"text":"Which enzyme is primarily responsible for unwinding the DNA double helix during DNA replication?","image":"","options":["DNA ligase","RNA polymerase","DNA helicase","DNA polymerase"],"correctIdx":2},{"text":"Which philosopher wrote Critique of Pure Reason?","image":"","options":["Georg Hegel","Immanuel Kant","John Locke","David Hume"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["Tom Hanks","Pedro Pascal","Tom Holland","Kevin Hart"],"correctIdx":1},{"text":"","image":"data:image/jpeg;base64,","options":["Venus de Milo","Olmec colossal heads","Manneken Pis","Easter Island's moais"],"correctIdx":3}]}